---
// No insurance or can't afford a doctor (#478, rank 3 in #475). A free clinic,
// sliding fee care, applying for coverage, and help with hospital bills. Every
// fact is in a resource record in content/resources/, read 2026-10-30.
// Health coverage is a high-stakes topic: the PR waits for David (#97).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import DateChip from '../components/DateChip.astro';
import { fixFormUrl } from '../lib/group-requests.mjs';
import ResourceCard from '../components/ResourceCard.astro';
import SourceLine from '../components/SourceLine.astro';
import { loadDir } from '../lib/content.mjs';
export const page = { door: "care", topic: "health", label: "No insurance or can't afford a doctor", summary: "A free clinic, sliding fee care, signing up for coverage, help with hospital bills" };
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const all = loadDir('resources');
const r = (slug) => all.find((e) => e.slug === slug);
const calendar = loadDir('calendar');
const open = calendar.find((e) => e.slug === 'marketplace-open-enrollment-2027');
// Price estimates and bill disputes without insurance (#1534), read 2026-11-02.
const gfe = [
  { url: 'https://www.cms.gov/medical-bill-rights/help/guides/good-faith-estimate', checked: '2026-11-02', name: 'CMS, Medical bill rights: good faith estimate' },
  { url: 'https://www.cms.gov/medical-bill-rights/help/dispute-a-bill', checked: '2026-11-02', name: 'CMS, Medical bill rights: dispute a bill' },
];
// Who WVCHIP covers and its income limits (#1534, need 2 gap), read 2026-11-14.
const chip = [
  { url: 'https://chip.wv.gov/eligibility', checked: '2026-11-14', name: 'WVCHIP, Eligibility' },
  { url: 'https://chip.wv.gov/co-payment-information', checked: '2026-11-14', name: 'WVCHIP, Co-Payment Information' },
  { url: 'https://chip.wv.gov/invoicing-monthly-premiums-resumed-december-2025', checked: '2026-11-14', name: 'WVCHIP, Invoicing for monthly premiums' },
];
---
<Base help title="No insurance or can't afford a doctor in Morgantown and Mon County" description="Health care with no insurance in Mon County, WV: the free Health Right clinic, sliding fee care, applying for Medicaid, free sign-up help, and help with hospital bills.">
  <h1>No insurance, or can't afford a doctor?</h1>
  <p class="lede">Low income and no insurance? Start with Milan Puskar Health Right, a free clinic in Morgantown. Call <a href="tel:3042928234">304-292-8234</a>. Below: care with a sliding fee, how to apply for Medicaid or other coverage, and help with a hospital bill.</p>

  <h2>A free clinic</h2>
  {r('health-right-clinic') && <ResourceCard r={r('health-right-clinic')} />}

  <h2>Care with a sliding fee</h2>
  <p>A sliding fee means you pay less when your income is lower.</p>
  {r('clay-battelle-health-center') && <ResourceCard r={r('clay-battelle-health-center')} showCost />}
  {r('monchd-clinical-services') && <ResourceCard r={r('monchd-clinical-services')} showCost />}

  <h2>Get health coverage</h2>
  {r('apply-for-medicaid-wv') && <ResourceCard r={r('apply-for-medicaid-wv')} />}
  {r('wv-navigator') && <ResourceCard r={r('wv-navigator')} />}
  <h3 id="wvchip">Health coverage for kids: who WVCHIP covers</h3>
  <p>WVCHIP is West Virginia's health coverage for children. A child can get it if the child:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>lives in West Virginia and is under 19,</li>
    <li>can't get West Virginia Medicaid,</li>
    <li>is a U.S. citizen or qualified immigrant (a child who is not a citizen needs proof of status), and</li>
    <li>is in a family whose income fits the limits below.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Family size is the number of people on your federal tax return. Income is your taxable income before taxes. Apply the same way as for Medicaid, above.</p>
  <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-labelledby="wvchip-income-cap" tabindex="0"><table>
    <caption id="wvchip-income-cap">WVCHIP: most a family can earn each month before taxes, by plan</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Family size</th><th scope="col">Gold</th><th scope="col">Blue</th><th scope="col">Premium</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">2</th><td>$2,705</td><td>$3,806</td><td>$5,410</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">3</th><td>$3,415</td><td>$4,804</td><td>$6,830</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">4</th><td>$4,125</td><td>$5,803</td><td>$8,250</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">5</th><td>$4,835</td><td>$6,802</td><td>$9,670</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">6</th><td>$5,545</td><td>$7,800</td><td>$11,090</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">7</th><td>$6,255</td><td>$8,799</td><td>$12,510</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Gold</strong> has copays only for some office visits and brand name medicines.</li>
    <li><strong>Blue</strong> adds copays for hospital care and emergency room visits.</li>
    <li><strong>Premium</strong> adds copays for some dental care, and a monthly payment: $35 a month for one child, or $71 a month for two or more. WVCHIP says coverage will not be closed for a late or missed payment.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="note">Children in a federally recognized American Indian or Alaska Native tribe pay no copays. A bigger family, or a question about these limits? Call the WVCHIP helpline at <a href="tel:18779822447">1-877-982-2447</a>. Over the limit? WV Navigator, above, helps you find other coverage.</p>
  <SourceLine sources={chip} about="who WVCHIP covers, its income limits, copays and premiums" />

  {open && <p>Marketplace plans for 2027: you can sign up at HealthCare.gov from November 1 to January 15. See <a href={`${base}/calendar/`}>Deadlines and dates</a> for the last day to sign up for coverage that starts January 1.</p>}
  <DateChip slug="marketplace-open-enrollment-2027" label="Marketplace sign-up" />
  <DateChip slug="marketplace-deadline-jan-1-coverage-2027" label="Last day for coverage that starts January 1" />

  <h2>Got a hospital bill you can't pay?</h2>
  <p>Both Morgantown hospitals have programs that can lower or cancel a bill for people who qualify.</p>
  {r('wvu-medicine-financial-assistance') && <ResourceCard r={r('wvu-medicine-financial-assistance')} />}
  {r('mon-health-charity-care') && <ResourceCard r={r('mon-health-charity-care')} />}

  <h3 id="estimate">Paying on your own? Ask for a price estimate first</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Get it in writing.</strong> Medicare's agency says that "if you aren't using health insurance to pay for your care," a provider must give you a good faith estimate of the cost when you ask, or when you schedule care at least 3 business days ahead.</li>
    <li><strong>Keep it.</strong> "You can't dispute your bill without an estimate."</li>
    <li><strong>If the bill is much higher,</strong> you can ask for an outside review when a provider charged at least $400 more than the estimate. You need a bill dated within the last 120 days and a $25 fee, which comes off what you owe if you win.</li>
    <li><strong>Questions?</strong> Call the No Surprises Help Desk at <a href="tel:18009853059">1-800-985-3059</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <SourceLine sources={gfe} about="good faith estimates and bill disputes" />

  <h2>Also check</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A dentist, or help paying for medicine: <a href={`${base}/dental-and-prescriptions/`}>dentist and prescription help</a>.</li>
    <li>On Medicare: <a href={`${base}/turning-65/`}>Turning 65 or on Medicare</a>, including help paying Medicare costs.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="meta">Sources checked October 30 and 31, 2026. We describe these programs; each one decides who qualifies. Call first, since hours and rules change. Something out of date? <a href={fixFormUrl({ page: Astro.url.pathname })}>Tell us</a>.</p>
</Base>
